  "created": "2026-10-28T16:33:56.563Z",
  "description": "EvoPdf Next RTF to PDF Converter for .NET (Multi-platform) is a component of the EvoPdf Next Library for .NET that enables accurate conversion of complex RTF documents to PDF.\n\nThe converter targets .NET Standard 2.0 and can be used in .NET Core and .NET Framework applications deployed on Windows and Linux, including Azure, AWS, Google Cloud, Docker and Kubernetes.\n\nThis multi-platform metapackage installs the Windows x64 and Linux x64 runtimes.\n\nFor Windows ARM64, Linux ARM64 and macOS ARM64, the additional packages EvoPdf.Next.RtfToPdf.Windows.Arm64, EvoPdf.Next.RtfToPdf.Linux.Arm64 and EvoPdf.Next.RtfToPdf.MacOS can be referenced on their own or alongside this package.\n\nCompatibility:\n\n* Windows 10, 11 and Windows Server 2016 to 2025 (x64)\n* Linux (x64) - Debian 11+, Ubuntu 20.04+ or equivalent\n* Windows, Linux and macOS (ARM64) - via additional packages\n* .NET 10.0, 9.0, 8.0, 7.0, 6.0 and .NET Standard 2.0\n* .NET Framework 4.6.2 to 4.8.1\n* Azure, AWS and Google Cloud\n* Virtual Machines\n* Docker containers and Kubernetes\n* Web, Console and Desktop applications\n\nMain Features:\n\n* Convert RTF documents from memory or from a file to PDF\n* Convert RTF content from .NET strings to PDF\n* Use custom PDF page settings to automatically reflow the content\n* Automatically create a table of contents based on headings in RTF\n* Add HTML headers, footers or stamps to the generated PDF\n* Control the PDF document display with PDF viewer preferences\n* Encrypt, set permissions and set passwords for the generated PDF documents\n* Add digital signatures to the generated PDF document\n* Asynchronous methods for async and await\n\nDocumentation and code samples:\nhttps://www.evopdf.com/evopdf-next-rtf-to-pdf-dotnet",
